\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Glory be to God on high,
\par And peace on earth descend:
\par God comes down, He bows the sky,
\par And shows Himself our Friend:
\par God the invisible appears:
\par God, the blest, the great I AM,
\par Sojourns in this vale of tears,
\par And Jesus is His name. 
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Him the angels all adored,
\par Their Maker and their King;
\par Tidings of their humbled Lord
\par They now to mortals bring.
\par Emptied of His majesty,
\par Of His dazzling glories shorn,
\par Being's source begins to be,
\par And God Himself is born!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. See the eternal Son of God
\par A mortal Son of Man;
\par Dwelling in an earthly clod,
\par Whom heaven cannot contain.
\par Stand amazed, ye heavens, at this:
\par See the Lord of earth and skies;
\par Humbled to the dust He is,
\par And in a manger lies.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. We, the sons of men, rejoice,
\par The Prince of Peace proclaim;
\par With heaven's host lift up our voice,
\par And shout Immanuel's name:
\par Knees and hearts to Him we bow;
\par Of our flesh and of our bone,
\par Jesus is our Brother now,
\par And God is all our own.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

